# SYNTHETIC fixture, and DERIVED: every line below is copied byte for byte
# from ~/code/sparqlwatch-runs/run-2026-08-24T19-45-03Z-lod-cloud-543.nq, the
# project's first registry-scale sweep, which is 6.3 MB and deliberately not in
# git (see that directory's README.md). This file is a strict LINE SUBSET of
# it, in the same order: the run's seven header quads, the whole chunk of nine
# of its 543 endpoints, and its two footer quads. Nothing was rewritten, so the
# run IRI, the prov:generatedAtTime, the verdicts and the elapsed times are the
# real sweep's, and every quad here appears verbatim in that file.
#
# Why a subset rather than the whole run: 6.3 MB in git for a test that needs
# nine rows. Why nine and not one: the index groups every endpoint by its
# availability verdict, so a fixture has to hold more than one group, and the
# chips have to carry more than one verdict or a page that drew every chip the
# same way would pass.
#
# The nine were chosen to cover every verdict value the sweep produced. In
# chunk order, with the availability verdict first because that is what the
# index groups by:
#
#   http://visualdataweb.infor.uva.es/sparql
#       indeterminate, and every other metric indeterminate too. This is the
#       modal row of the sweep: 402 of the 543 look exactly like it.
#   https://data.ascdc.tw/en/sparql.php
#       indeterminate, cors-preflight absent, the rest indeterminate. The
#       mixed non-responder row, and 52 of the 543 look like this, which is
#       why "the endpoints that show indeterminate" is not a set.
#   https://data.epo.org/linked-data/query
#       verified, geo-functions declared-but-wrong, cors-preflight and
#       service-description absent. declared-but-wrong is the only verdict
#       that asserts an error, and this is the sweep's only endpoint carrying
#       it beside two absent chips.
#   https://www.foodie-cloud.org/sparql
#       verified, and the sweep's only endpoint whose every metric is either
#       verified or undeclared-but-verified.
#   http://caligraph.org/sparql
#       indeterminate, service-description verified, cors absent.
#   https://sparql.uniprot.org/sparql
#       verified, with cors, cors-preflight and has-classes verified and
#       geo-data absent. A responder whose row still carries an absent chip.
#   https://purl.org/whonto/onto
#       absent, one of only four in the sweep, with cors and cors-preflight
#       absent as well.
#   https://dbpedia.org/page/Summer_Olympic_Games
#       indeterminate, with cors-preflight VERIFIED: a non-responder can still
#       carry a verified chip, because the metrics are independent.
#   https://raw.githubusercontent.com/GVogeler/bookkeeping/master/bookkeeping.ttl
#       absent, the second of the sweep's four here, and cors verified beside
#       it. A .ttl file rather than a SPARQL endpoint: the host answered, with
#       something that was not a SPARQL result, which is what absent means.
#
# So the availability verdicts are 3 verified, 4 indeterminate and 2 absent,
# and the verdict values across all metrics are verified,
# undeclared-but-verified, declared-but-wrong, indeterminate and absent.
# declared-only appears nowhere, in this file or in the 543-endpoint sweep it
# was cut from.
#
# What it does NOT hold, on purpose: an endpoint with no availability verdict
# at all. That is run-prober-failed.nq, which is a whole run of exactly that
# shape, and web/tests/conftest.py loads the two together rather than merging
# them into one file. There is also no content sample anywhere here, because
# the sweep ran at the cheap ceiling and declined sw:metric:classes for every
# one of the 543, which is why each endpoint here carries seven measurements
# and one cost-ceiling decline.
#
# 462 quads, one run graph (urn:sparqlwatch:run:2026-08-24T19:45:03Z), nine
# endpoints, 63 dqv:QualityMeasurement resources, 9 sw:NotMeasured resources,
# no sw:ContentSample. The run finished, so its footer's sw:finalised is here,
# and its sw:failedEndpoints "0" is as true of these nine as it was of the
# whole sweep. The subjects are the derived scheme of stage 1c-b3.
